desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Use of MD5 in Kotlin"
	title_zh: "Kotlin 中使用 MD5"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-use-of-md5-kotlin"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `use-of-md5` (kotlin/lang/security/use-of-md5.yaml).
Original message: Detected MD5 hash algorithm which is considered insecure. MD5 is not collision resistant and is therefore not suitable as a cryptographic signature. Use SHA256 or SHA3 instead.
CWE: CWE-328: Use of Weak Hash
References:
- https://owasp.org/Top10/A02_2021-Cryptographic_Failures
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.kt": <<<POS
java.security.MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5")
POS
	"safefile://pos.kt": <<<NEG
MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256")
NEG
)

${*.kt}.pattern_regex(/(?:java\.security\.MessageDigest\.getInstance\("MD5"\))|(?:org\.apache\.commons\.codec\.digest\.DigestUtils\.getMd5Digest\(\))/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Use of MD5 in Kotlin",
	title_zh: "Kotlin 中使用 MD5",
	message: "Use of MD5 detected.",
}
